{#
  The app, running, in the page.

  Not a video and not a screenshot: a real script, scrolling at real
  lines-per-minute, with the cues in the cue colour and the clock counting up,
  exactly as the phone does it. The lines come from _data/deck.js, and each
  page passes its own set in as `deckScript` — a page about filming on TikTok
  should not be running a script about a Zoom call, and forty-two pages should
  not be running the same eleven sentences as each other.

  script.js drives it; with no JavaScript it sits still and is simply a picture
  of the app, which is fine, because that is what a screenshot would have been.

  It is also the hero's argument in one object: you can see the words move,
  see a cue go past without being read out, and see the timer run.
#}
<div class="deck reveal d2" data-deck>
    <div class="deck-bar">
        <span class="deck-close" aria-hidden="true">✕</span>
        <span class="deck-title">Teleprompter</span>
        <span class="deck-clock" data-deck-clock>00:00</span>
    </div>

    <div class="deck-screen">
        <div class="deck-script" data-deck-script>
            {% for l in (deckScript or deck.standard) %}
            <p class="deck-line{% if l.cue %} is-cue{% endif %}">{{ l.cue or l.t }}</p>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="deck-controls">
        <button class="deck-btn deck-btn-main" type="button" data-deck-toggle aria-label="Pause the prompter">Pause</button>
        <button class="deck-btn" type="button" data-deck-restart aria-label="Start the script again">Restart</button>
        <span class="deck-speed">
            <label for="deck-speed">Speed</label>
            <input id="deck-speed" type="range" min="12" max="60" step="2" value="26" data-deck-speed
                   aria-label="Scroll speed in lines per minute">
        </span>
    </div>
</div>
<p class="deck-legend reveal d3">The <b>pink lines are cues</b>, written for you to read and not to say, and the <b>clock at the top</b> is the timer counting how long you have been talking.</p>
